    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· Baguette Bag ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/cqy0o60/cf4557a01beeac42.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/cqy0o60/cf4557a01beeac42.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Launched in 1997, the Baguette was designed and named by Silvia Venturini Fendi, one of the FENDI family heirs. The name, French for \"baguette\" bread, directly describes the bag's key characteristic: thanks to its short shoulder strap and distinctive elongated shape, when worn, it looks as if the wearer is carrying a small baguette fresh from the bakery—effortlessly chic and elegant.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Upon its release, the Baguette sparked a frenzy among fashion circles and remains a true evergreen in the FENDI bag family. In 2000, Carrie Bradshaw, the protagonist of the hit TV series *Sex and the City*, elevated the Baguette from a cult favorite to a must-have on everyone's wish list.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/cqy0o60/889d080f880359c2.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/cqy0o60/889d080f880359c2.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Madonna carrying the Baguette at the 2000 BAFTA Awards dinner",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
